    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (there's a single black-box acceptance test class that exercises the `POST /api/owners` endpoint). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the shared-household feature so that setting `sharesHousehold: true` on owner creation assigns and returns a stable, shared `householdId`.\n\n**What the change does**\n- When a new owner's last name + address already belong to an existing owner (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace):\n  - If `sharesHousehold` is **not** true \u2192 still rejected with **409** (unchanged behavior).\n  - If `sharesHousehold` is **true** \u2192 the create is allowed, and the joiner *and* all existing household members are assigned the **same `householdId`**, which is returned on read.\n- The `householdId` is derived deterministically (first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over the normalized last name + address), so every member of a household resolves to the same value \u2014 a genuinely stable shared identifier. It's absent for owners not sharing a household.\n\n**Files changed**\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 replaced `rejectDuplicateHousehold` with `applyHousehold`, which computes the shared id (`generateHouseholdId`), sets it on the new owner, and back-fills existing housemates. Added the SHA-256 imports.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter; MapStruct auto-maps it to the DTO.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column.\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 extended the positional seed inserts (used by the test profile) with the new column's `NULL`.\n\nVerified: `AcceptanceTest.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
